{'symbol': 'ALL', 'date': '2020-09-30 18:30:00', 'title': 'ALLSTATE SAYS RESTRUCTURING PLAN THAT WILL IMPACT ABOUT 3,800 EMPLOYEES IS BEING IMPLEMENTED', 'text': 'ALLSTATE CORP - ANNOUNCES EXPECTED THIRD QUARTER RESTRUCTURING AND OTHER CHARGES.ALLSTATE CORP - TO LOWER COSTS, A RESTRUCTURING PLAN IS BEING IMPLEMENTED WHICH WILL IMPACT ABOUT 3,800 EMPLOYEES.ALLSTATE - EXPECTS TO INCUR RESTRUCTURING CHARGE OF ABOUT $290 MILLION, PRE-TAX, WITH ABOUT $210 MILLION TO $220 MILLION, PRE-TAX, TO BE RECOGNIZED DURING Q3 2020.ALLSTATE - EXPECTS TO INCUR  RESTRUCTURING CHARGE OF $50 MILLION TO $60 MILLION, PRE-TAX, TO BE RECOGNIZED IN Q4, ANY REMAINING CHARGES TO BE RECOGNIZED IN H1 2021.ALLSTATE - ADDITIONALLY, EXPECTS TO INCUR REAL ESTATE EXIT COSTS OF ABOUT $80 MILLION, PRE-TAX, RESULTING FROM OFFICE CLOSURES.'}